<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">22022026</say-as>.</s> <s>It's just past six in the evening in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈmæk.kæ">Makkah</phoneme>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>Iran has fortified its nuclear sites and placed a senior military commander in charge of war preparations, even as Tehran and Washington confirmed they will hold fresh nuclear talks in early March.</s> <s>Satellite images show hardened tunnel entrances at the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="nɑːˈtɑːnz">Natanz</phoneme> enrichment facility, and United States strike forces are expected to be in position by mid-March.</s> <s>The two sides remain far apart, with Tehran demanding the lifting of all sanctions and Washington offering only partial relief.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In conflict and security.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Pakistani airstrikes struck two provinces inside Afghanistan on Saturday, with Kabul reporting that the attacks killed civilians including children after hitting a school and homes in residential areas.</s> <s>Islamabad said it was targeting Pakistani Taliban camps in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="næŋˈɡɑːr.hɑːr">Nangarhar</phoneme> and <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈpæk.tɪ.kɑː">Paktika</phoneme>.</s> <s>Afghanistan's Taliban government promised a measured response, warning that continued strikes could collapse a fragile ceasefire that has held since October.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Russia launched a barrage of ballistic missiles and drones against Kyiv before dawn on Saturday, striking homes across five districts of the Ukrainian capital and wounding dozens of people.</s> <s>The attack came two days before the fourth anniversary of the full-scale invasion, with the war now entering its fifth year.</s> <s>No ceasefire talks are scheduled, and both sides show no sign of breaking the military stalemate.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Israeli settlers declared a new settlement deep inside Hebron on Saturday, seizing five Palestinian-owned buildings in a densely populated neighbourhood after Israeli soldiers had arrested dozens of residents.</s> <s>The settlers vowed not to wait for government authorization, and the legality of the takeover is contested under international law.</s> <s>Fourteen nations have condemned recent remarks by the United States ambassador that appeared to endorse settler expansion in the occupied city.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The unrecognized territory of Somaliland has offered Washington lithium, coltan, and access to Red Sea military bases in exchange for United States diplomatic recognition.</s> <s>A senior Somaliland minister made the terms public, describing the territory's mineral reserves and strategic coastline as significant negotiating leverage.</s> <s>President Trump signalled last August he was considering the offer, but no formal response has come from Washington.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Brazil's President Lula challenged Washington on trade while visiting New Delhi, calling on the United States to treat all countries equally.</s> <s>He signed critical minerals agreements with India's Prime Minister Modi as part of a broader South-South effort to reduce reliance on American markets and supply chains.</s> <s>Lula is due to meet President Trump in Washington next month, with forty percent tariffs on Brazilian exports still in force.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>North Korea's leader Kim Jong Un opened the Workers' Party Congress in Pyongyang, outlining military and economic goals for the country through 2031.</s> <s>He claimed radical successes despite international sanctions, convening the congress — held only every five years — with delegates assembled to endorse the full programme.</s> <s>The complete five-year plan, expected to include expanded weapons and economic targets, will be published when the congress concludes.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>The European Parliament approved a landmark trade deal between the European Union and South America's <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˌmɛr.koʊˈsʊər">Mercosur</phoneme> bloc, attaching agricultural safeguards that allow Brussels to suspend tariff benefits if farm imports rise by five percent.</s> <s>Four hundred and eighty-three members voted in favour.</s> <s>Argentina's government backed the deal despite the caps, urgently seeking new markets as American tariffs foreclose alternatives for its exporters.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Indonesia has secured a bilateral trade agreement with the United States, agreeing to remove tariffs on ninety-nine percent of American goods in exchange for exemptions covering nearly two thousand Indonesian export lines at a nineteen percent rate.</s> <s>President <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈprɑː.bo.wo">Prabowo</phoneme> announced the agreement after talks in Washington.</s> <s>Other Southeast Asian nations still face American tariffs with no comparable bilateral deal of their own.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A randomized controlled trial published in Nature found that nearly five thousand users of the social platform X shifted measurably to the right after seven weeks on its algorithmic feed.</s> <s>Participants assigned to the algorithm rather than a chronological feed showed changes in their views on policy, Trump, and the war in Ukraine.</s> <s>Those shifts persisted after users switched back, as the algorithm had already nudged them into following right-leaning accounts.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A botnet assembled from millions of hacked devices overwhelmed the Invisible Internet Project, a privacy network relied on by journalists and activists in countries with restricted internet access, outnumbering its nodes thirty-nine to one.</s> <s>The botnet's operators had lost control of their command servers and rerouted traffic through the network, flooding it with illegitimate connections.</s> <s>Developers restored service and rolled out post-quantum encryption within six days.</s>
<break time="900ms"/>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>An artificial intelligence system called DeepRare, published in Nature, outperformed specialist doctors in diagnosing rare diseases across nearly three thousand conditions.</s> <s>The system uses forty specialized tools and generates traceable reasoning that medical experts verified as correct ninety-five percent of the time.</s> <s>Three hundred million people living with rare diseases typically spend more than five years without an accurate diagnosis before receiving one.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A study in Nature has found that rising atmospheric carbon dioxide is depleting nitrogen in boreal forests, undermining their capacity to absorb carbon.</s> <s>Analysis of Swedish forest tree rings from 1961 to 2018 showed that higher carbon dioxide drives faster growth, stripping nitrogen from the soil and locking it in plant litter.</s> <s>Climate models that rely on these northern forests as a growing carbon sink may be significantly overestimating their capacity.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
<break time="500ms"/>
<s>We're back in one hour.</s>
<break time="300ms"/>
<s><phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ʔɪn ʃæːʔ ɑɫ.ɫɑːh">إن شاء الله</phoneme>.</s>
</speak>